Rules:
{"id": "RULE-001", "name": "Only current, savings and virtual accounts can be debited", "category": "validation", "statement": "A payment order can only be paid from an account of type CTE (current), AHO (savings) or VIR (virtual). Any other account type is rejected with error 50001 'TIPO DE CUENTA NO PERMITIDO'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:34-39"]}
{"id": "RULE-002", "name": "Order must exist and be pending", "category": "lifecycle", "statement": "The payment order, identified by order number and company, must exist and be in state 'P' (pending). A missing order gives error 50002 'ORDEN NO EXISTE'. An order in any other state gives error 50003 'ORDEN NO ESTA PENDIENTE', so an order cannot be paid twice.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:42-59"]}
{"id": "RULE-003", "name": "Service tariff lookup: company tariff first, then general service tariff", "category": "policy", "statement": "The tariff for the service is taken from the company-specific tariff table, together with its 'charged separately' flag. If the company has no tariff for the service, the general service tariff is used and the commission is never charged separately ('N'). A missing tariff value is treated as 0.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:62-77"]}
{"id": "RULE-004", "name": "Commission by channel; payroll is exempt", "category": "calculation", "statement": "Orders from the WEB channel pay half of the tariff, rounded to 2 decimals. Other channels pay the full tariff. The NOMINA (payroll) service never pays commission.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:80-86"]}
{"id": "RULE-005", "name": "Total to debit includes the commission unless it is charged separately", "category": "calculation", "statement": "If the commission is flagged as separate ('S'), the first debit is only the order value. Otherwise the commission is added and the account is debited for value plus commission.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:89-92"]}
{"id": "RULE-006", "name": "Funds check: no overdraft on virtual accounts, 100.00 overdraft on others", "category": "validation", "statement": "A virtual account (VIR) must have a balance of at least the total to debit. Current and savings accounts may be overdrawn by up to 100.00, so balance + 100.00 must cover the total. Otherwise the payment is rejected with error 50004 'FONDOS INSUFICIENTES'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:95-106"]}
{"id": "RULE-007", "name": "Debit of the account for the payment", "category": "lifecycle", "statement": "Inside a transaction, the account is debited for the total with reference 'PAGO ORDEN', and the movement number is returned to the caller. If the debit fails, the transaction is rolled back and the payment fails with error 50005 'ERROR EN DEBITO'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:108-123"]}
{"id": "RULE-008", "name": "A separate commission is debited as a second movement", "category": "calculation", "statement": "When the commission is charged separately and is greater than zero, it is debited as its own movement with reference 'COMISION PAGO'. If that debit fails, the whole transaction, including the payment debit, is rolled back with error 50006 'ERROR EN COMISION'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:126-141"]}
{"id": "RULE-009", "name": "Order is marked paid with payment date and commission", "category": "lifecycle", "statement": "After the debits, the order moves from pending to paid ('A'), recording the processing date as payment date and the commission charged. If the update fails or touches no row, everything is rolled back with error 50007 'ERROR ACTUALIZANDO ORDEN'. Otherwise the transaction is committed and the message is 'PAGO REALIZADO'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:144-164"]}
